## Design Decision: No Hardcoded Equipment Limits

All thresholds that control equipment are user-configurable via Web UI. The only non-configurable values are physical safety limits (`SAFETY_HUM_CEILING_HARD` at 95%) that act as emergency brakes — they don't control normal operation, they prevent disaster.

---

## Design Decision: Alert Rate Limiting

`network_sendAlert()` enforces `NTFY_MIN_INTERVAL_MS` (60s) globally. Alive pings reuse this function and inherit the rate limiting automatically. Critical alerts and alive pings share the same cooldown — alive pings fire every 30 min so collision is unlikely, but if both queue simultaneously, rate limiting applies. The alive ping runs in `loop()` via `network_sendAlivePing()` with WiFi connectivity guard and immediate-first-ping-on-boot logic.

---

## Design Decision: Dormant-by-Default Features

Two v1.4 features ship dormant to prevent unintended behavior on existing installs:
- **`NTFY_ENABLED`** defaults to `false` — alive pings won't fire until the user sets this to `true` and configures their ntfy.sh endpoint
- **`DEFAULT_HUM_EXHAUST_ON`** defaults to `95.0f` (equal to `SAFETY_HUM_CEILING_HARD`) — the high-humidity exhaust won't trigger independently until the user lowers it via Web UI (recommended: 92%)

